{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_01FrzYYtVHdmUnLHsf6HGq2Z","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Here's what was completed:\n\n**✅ Q10 written:** `ai-engineering/answers/07-010-model-tiering-small-distilled-vs-large-llm.md`\n\nKey content in the answer:\n- **Concept:** Route 60–80% of low-complexity queries to cheap models (GPT-4o-mini at $0.15/M, Llama 3 8B self-hosted) and reserve frontier models (GPT-4o at $2.50/M) for the hard 5–10%\n- **Mechanism:** 5-step design — profile query distribution → build a lightweight complexity router (DistilBERT or rules-based, <5ms) → define 3 tiers → validate on golden set (must be within ~3pt quality gap) → monitor per-tier drift in production\n- **Concrete math:** 500K queries/day customer support chatbot: naive all-GPT-4o → $1,000/day; tiered routing → $85/day (92% reduction)\n- **Pitfalls:** Routing everything to small model without a classifier; using leaderboard scores instead of task-specific golden-set eval; ignoring router latency overhead\n- **Self-hosting angle:** Break-even at ~$20–50K/month API spend\n\n**6 items remaining in Next** (Q11–Q16 + validate)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":337,"cache_read_input_tokens":76704,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":337,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1a6157f8-419c-43fb-bd14-ddbcc46d7f87","uuid":"d542c445-42fe-4b56-9daf-76eb63694155"}
